## Readmission Risk Model

### Purpose
Predicts the probability of hospital readmission within 30 days of discharge.

### Model Details

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Algorithm | Gradient Boosted Trees (XGBoost) |
| Training Data | 2.5M discharges (2020-2024) |
| Features | 156 |
| AUC-ROC | 0.82 |
| Precision @10% | 0.45 |
| Recall @10% | 0.38 |

### Feature Categories

| Category | Features | Importance |
|----------|----------|------------|
| Prior Utilization | 28 | 32% |
| Clinical Indicators | 45 | 28% |
| Demographics | 12 | 8% |
| Social Factors | 18 | 15% |
| Medications | 32 | 12% |
| Discharge Factors | 21 | 5% |

### Top Features

| Rank | Feature | Importance |
|------|---------|------------|
| 1 | Prior 30-day readmissions (12mo) | 8.5% |
| 2 | Length of stay | 6.2% |
| 3 | ED visits (6mo) | 5.8% |
| 4 | Charlson Comorbidity Index | 5.4% |
| 5 | Discharge disposition | 4.9% |
| 6 | Age | 4.2% |
| 7 | Number of active medications | 3.8% |
| 8 | Primary diagnosis category | 3.5% |
| 9 | Insurance type | 3.2% |
| 10 | Social isolation score | 2.9% |

### Risk Tiers

| Tier | Score Range | % Population | Readmit Rate |
|------|-------------|--------------|--------------|
| Very High | 0.70 - 1.00 | 5% | 42% |
| High | 0.50 - 0.69 | 12% | 28% |
| Medium | 0.30 - 0.49 | 25% | 15% |
| Low | 0.10 - 0.29 | 35% | 8% |
| Very Low | 0.00 - 0.09 | 23% | 3% |

### API Usage

```http
GET /analytics/patients/{patientId}/risk/readmission

Response:
{
  "patientId": "pat_abc123",
  "modelVersion": "3.2",
  "score": 0.68,
  "tier": "HIGH",
  "confidence": 0.92,
  "topFactors": [
    {"factor": "Prior readmission in 90 days", "contribution": 0.15},
    {"factor": "Heart failure diagnosis", "contribution": 0.12},
    {"factor": "Polypharmacy (12+ meds)", "contribution": 0.08}
  ],
  "calculatedAt": "2025-01-17T10:30:00Z"
}
```

