## Clinical Deterioration Model

### Purpose
Predicts risk of clinical deterioration requiring escalation of care within 24-48 hours.

### Model Details

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Algorithm | LSTM Neural Network |
| Training Data | 800K patient-days |
| Features | 48 (time-series) |
| AUC-ROC | 0.85 |
| Precision @5% | 0.52 |
| Sensitivity | 0.78 |

### Input Features

| Category | Features |
|----------|----------|
| Vital Signs | HR, BP, RR, SpO2, Temp |
| Labs | BMP, CBC, Lactate, Troponin |
| Nursing Assessments | Pain, LOC, Mobility |
| Trends | 4hr, 8hr, 24hr deltas |
| Context | Age, diagnosis, floor |

### Alert Thresholds

| Threshold | Score | Action |
|-----------|-------|--------|
| Critical | >0.80 | Immediate escalation |
| High | 0.60-0.79 | MD notification |
| Moderate | 0.40-0.59 | Increased monitoring |
| Low | <0.40 | Standard care |

