## Risk Stratification Model

### Purpose
Assigns patients to risk tiers for population health management and resource allocation.

### Model Details

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Algorithm | Ensemble (RF + XGBoost + LR) |
| Training Data | 5M patients |
| Features | 212 |
| AUC-ROC | 0.80 |
| Segments | 5 |

### Risk Segments

| Segment | % Population | Characteristics |
|---------|--------------|-----------------|
| Rising Risk | 15% | 2+ chronic conditions, recent utilization |
| High Cost | 5% | Top 5% spend, complex conditions |
| Chronic Stable | 25% | Managed chronic conditions |
| Healthy | 45% | Low utilization, few conditions |
| Emerging | 10% | Early warning signs |

### Use Cases

| Use Case | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Care Management | Prioritize outreach |
| Resource Planning | Staff allocation |
| Intervention Targeting | Program eligibility |
| Financial Forecasting | Budget planning |

